  "gHowTitle": "How it works",
  "gHowSubtitle": "The whole setup at a glance",
  "gHowLead": "GameTranslator links three devices. The game runs on the PS5, you play on the TV, and the phone translates in between:",
  "gHowStep1": "The phone takes the game picture from the PS5 over Remote Play. No camera is used.",
  "gHowStep2": "It reads the area of the picture where the subtitles appear and translates the text.",
  "gHowStep3": "It sends the translation to the TV on the same Wi-Fi. The GameTranslator app on the TV shows it over the game.",
  "gHowNeedsTitle": "What you need",
  "gHowNeed1": "A PS5 with a second user on it (explained below).",
  "gHowNeed2": "A TV with the GameTranslator TV app installed: LG, Samsung or Android TV / Google TV.",
  "gHowNeed3": "One home network (Wi-Fi) that the phone, the PS5 and the TV are all connected to.",
  "gHowNeed4": "Internet for online translation. There is also an offline translation option.",
  "gHowTip": "Setup is done once. After that you only start translation and open the app on the TV.",
  "gPs5Title": "Prepare the PS5",
  "gPs5Subtitle": "A second user and Remote Play",
  "gPs5UserTitle": "1. Add a second user",
  "gPs5UserBody": "The PS5 treats the device that connects over Remote Play as that user's controller. If the phone connects with your account, your controller is detached from the TV. That is why the phone connects with a separate user; you keep playing on your own account.",
  "gPs5UserStep1": "Add a new user on the PS5 (from the profile picture on the home screen: Switch User › Add User).",
  "gPs5UserStep2": "Sign that user in with a PSN account. You can create one for free; PS Plus is not required.",
  "gPs5UserStep3": "You will also sign in to PSN on the phone with this second account.",
  "gPs5RemoteTitle": "2. Turn on Remote Play",
  "gPs5RemoteStep1": "Switch to the second user on the PS5.",
  "gPs5RemoteStep2": "Go to Settings › System › Remote Play.",
  "gPs5RemoteStep3": "Turn on \"Enable Remote Play\".",
  "gPs5WakeTitle": "3. Waking from rest mode (optional)",
  "gPs5WakeBody": "So the phone can wake the PS5 when you start translation while it is in rest mode:",
  "gPs5WakeStep1": "Go to Settings › System › Power Saving › Features Available in Rest Mode.",
  "gPs5WakeStep2": "Turn on \"Stay Connected to the Internet\" and \"Enable Turning On PS5 from Network\".",
  "gPs5Tip": "If you do not want waking, turn off Settings › PS5 › \"Wake if in rest mode\" on the phone.",
  "gPairTitle": "Pair the phone with the PS5",
  "gPairSubtitle": "PSN sign-in and the 8-digit code",
  "gPairSignInTitle": "1. Sign in with PSN",
  "gPairSignInStep1": "On the setup screen tap \"Sign in with PSN\". Sony's own sign-in page opens.",
  "gPairSignInStep2": "Sign in with the account of the second user on the PS5.",
  "gPairSignInStep3": "When sign-in finishes, the app returns to setup by itself and shows \"PSN account connected\".",
  "gPairSignInTip": "Your password goes straight to Sony; the app only stores your account ID.",
  "gPairCodeTitle": "2. Enter the pairing code",
  "gPairCodeStep1": "On the PS5, while the second user is active, go to Settings › System › Remote Play › \"Link Device\".",
  "gPairCodeStep2": "An 8-digit code and a countdown appear on the screen. The code is valid for about 5 minutes.",
  "gPairCodeStep3": "On the phone, pick your PS5 from the \"Found console\" list.",
  "gPairCodeStep4": "Type the code into the boxes and tap \"Pair\".",
  "gPairMissingTitle": "If the PS5 is not in the list",
  "gPairMissing1": "Check that the phone and the PS5 are on the same Wi-Fi network; it must not be a guest network or mobile data.",
  "gPairMissing2": "Tap \"Refresh\".",
  "gPairMissing3": "If it still does not appear, tap \"Enter the IP address manually\". The address is shown on the PS5 under Settings › Network › Connection Status › View Connection Status.",
  "gPairTip": "Pairing is done once. If the PS5 address changes, the app finds it again on the network.",
  "gTvTitle": "Prepare the TV",
  "gTvSubtitle": "Supported TVs and the TV app",
  "gTvLead": "A separate GameTranslator TV app shows the subtitles on the TV. It is not in the stores yet, so it is installed on the TV once. You can install it on LG and Android TV from this phone; on Samsung, installation is currently done from a computer.",
  "gTvSupportedTitle": "Which TVs are supported?",
  "gTvTableLg": "LG",
  "gTvTableLgDetail": "webOS 4 and later",
  "gTvTableSamsung": "Samsung",
  "gTvTableSamsungDetail": "Tizen, 2019 and later",
  "gTvTableAndroid": "Android TV / Google TV",
  "gTvTableAndroidDetail": "Vestel, Arçelik, Beko, Grundig, Philips, Sony, TCL and others",
  "gTvTableOther": "Others",
  "gTvTableOtherDetail": "Linux models from Vestel/Arçelik/Beko/Grundig, Philips Saphi, Titan OS",
  "gTvNotSupported": "Not supported: the app cannot be installed on these TVs.",
  "gTvAndroidTip": "Is your TV an Android TV? If the home screen says Google Play Store or \"Google TV\", it is.",
  "gTvLgTitle": "LG",
  "gTvLgStep1": "On a computer, create a free LG developer account at webostv.developer.lge.com.",
  "gTvLgStep2": "On the TV, install the \"Developer Mode\" app from LG Content Store, sign in with your account and turn on \"Dev Mode Status\". The TV restarts.",
  "gTvLgStep3": "In the Developer Mode app on the TV, turn on \"Key Server\".",
  "gTvLgStep4": "On the phone, choose LG in the \"Install the TV app\" wizard, find your TV and type the 6-character passphrase shown on the screen (the TV step of GameTranslator on a computer does the same).",
  "gTvLgNote": "On LG, developer mode stays on for at most 1000 hours. If you will not use it for a long time, press \"EXTEND\" in the Developer Mode app before the time runs out; once it expires the TV app is removed and you have to install it again.",
  "gTvSamsungTitle": "Samsung",
  "gTvSamsungStep1": "On the TV open the Apps screen and press 1 2 3 4 5 on the remote. The developer mode window opens.",
  "gTvSamsungStep2": "Turn on \"Developer mode\" and type your computer's address into \"Host PC IP\".",
  "gTvSamsungStep3": "Fully power the TV off and on by holding the power button.",
  "gTvSamsungStep4": "In the TV step of GameTranslator on the computer, select your TV. On the page that opens, sign in with a free Samsung account; the app is signed and installed.",
  "gTvAndroidTitle": "Android TV / Google TV",
  "gTvAndroidStep1": "On the TV go to Settings › Device Preferences › About (on Google TV: Settings › System › About).",
  "gTvAndroidStep2": "Press OK 7 times on \"Build\".",
  "gTvAndroidStep3": "In Developer options turn on \"USB debugging\" (and \"Network debugging\" if available).",
  "gTvAndroidStep4": "On the phone, choose \"Android TV / Google TV\" in the \"Install the TV app\" wizard and accept the prompt on the TV.",
  "gTvAndroidNote": "If the TV does not allow network debugging, you can also install with a USB drive: download the TV app APK from GameTranslator's releases page, copy it to the drive and open it with a file manager on the TV.",
  "gTvAfterTitle": "After installation",
  "gTvAfterBody": "The TV app finds the phone on the network by itself; you do not need to type the TV's address on the phone. On Samsung the computer is only needed for installation; afterwards it can stay off.",
  "gTvObsTitle": "For streamers: OBS",
  "gTvObsBody": "While translation is on, the subtitles are also served as a web page. In OBS add a \"Browser Source\" and use http://{phone}:8787/obs as the address (1920×1080). The page background is transparent; it does not show the subtitles over the game in the TV browser and is only meant for stream and recording layouts.",
