  "gFirstTitle": "First use",
  "gFirstSubtitle": "Start translation and see it on the TV",
  "gFirstStep1": "Open the game on the PS5 with your own account and turn on subtitles in the game settings.",
  "gFirstStep2": "Tap the big button on the phone's home screen. The first time you are asked for notification permission; allow it so translation can continue in the background.",
  "gFirstStep3": "When the status says \"Translation on\", the PS5 card says \"Connected\". The first connection takes a few seconds.",
  "gFirstStep4": "Open the GameTranslator app on the TV. Within a few seconds the TV card on the phone says \"Connected\".",
  "gFirstStep5": "If the TV shows no game picture, press OK to open the panel and use left/right to select the HDMI input the PS5 is connected to.",
  "gFirstStep6": "If there is no sound from the TV, the PS5 has routed audio to Remote Play: press the PS button, open Sound › Output Device from the menu at the bottom and choose HDMI. This is done once.",
  "gFirstStep7": "On the phone tap \"Send a test subtitle to the TV\". If you see the text on the TV, everything is ready.",
  "gFirstTip": "You can turn the phone screen off while translation is on. To stop, tap the button in the app or \"Stop\" in the notification.",
  "gFirstNextTitle": "Next time",
  "gFirstNextBody": "Only two steps: start translation on the phone, open GameTranslator on the TV.",
  "gFirstBatteryTitle": "Battery and heat",
  "gFirstBatteryBody": "The phone decodes video and reads text continuously; for long sessions keep it plugged in.",
  "gRemoteTitle": "TV remote",
  "gRemoteSubtitle": "The buttons in the TV app",
  "gRemoteLead": "While GameTranslator is open on the TV, the remote buttons do this:",
  "gRemoteOk": "OK",
  "gRemoteOkText": "Opens and closes the status panel (HDMI input, connection status).",
  "gRemoteLeftRight": "Left / Right",
  "gRemoteLeftRightText": "Changes the HDMI input while the panel is open.",
  "gRemoteNumbers": "1 – 4",
  "gRemoteNumbersText": "Selects the HDMI input directly.",
  "gRemoteUpDown": "Up / Down",
  "gRemoteUpDownText": "Moves the subtitle up or down on the screen.",
  "gRemoteRed": "Red",
  "gRemoteRedText": "Shows the TV's own test caption.",
  "gRemoteGreen": "Green",
  "gRemoteGreenText": "Opens and closes the status panel.",
  "gRemoteBlue": "Blue",
  "gRemoteBlueText": "Starts or stops the demo with sample subtitles.",
  "gRemoteBack": "Back",
  "gRemoteBackText": "Exits the app.",
  "gRemoteTip": "You play with the PS5 controller; the TV remote is only needed for these settings.",
  "gRegionTitle": "Adjust the subtitle region",
  "gRegionSubtitle": "Where the phone looks on the screen",
  "gRegionBody": "The phone reads only the area where the subtitles appear, not the whole screen. If the region is in the wrong place, no translation arrives or other text on the screen gets translated.",
  "gRegionStep1": "With translation on, wait for a subtitle to appear in the game.",
  "gRegionStep2": "Look at the blue frame in the preview on the home screen: the whole subtitle must be inside the frame.",
  "gRegionStep3": "If not, tap \"Adjust the subtitle region\". Pick the Top, Bottom, Left or Right edge and move it with the slider.",
  "gRegionStep4": "The \"Read in the frame\" line on the home screen shows what the phone reads at that moment; the whole subtitle should appear there.",
  "gRegionBullet1": "If the start or end of the sentence is cut off, widen the frame.",
  "gRegionBullet2": "If the top line of two-line subtitles disappears, move the top edge up.",
  "gRegionBullet3": "If other text such as objectives or map names is translated, narrow the frame.",
  "gRegionTip": "Every game puts subtitles in a different place; when you start a new game, one look at the region is enough.",
  "gLookTitle": "Translation and appearance",
  "gLookSubtitle": "Engine, glossary and the text on the TV",
  "gEngineTitle": "Translation engine",
  "gEngineGoogle": "Google",
  "gEngineGoogleText": "Needs internet, no key required. The best starting point for most games.",
  "gEngineDeepl": "DeepL",
  "gEngineDeeplText": "Builds more natural sentences. You need to enter your own API key from DeepL.",
  "gEngineOnDevice": "On device",
  "gEngineOnDeviceText": "Works offline; its quality is lower than the others. The language model downloads once on first use.",
  "gEngineFallback": "If the internet drops, translation switches to the on-device model by itself and switches back when the connection returns.",
  "gGlossaryTitle": "Glossary",
  "gGlossaryBody": "To pin character names and game terms that the translation gets wrong (English → Turkish only). Open it from Settings › Translation › Glossary. Terms in \"terms\" are translated to the text you write; names in \"keep\" stay as they are.",
  "gLookOnTvTitle": "Appearance on the TV",
  "gLookOnTv1": "Font size and color: Settings › On TV.",
  "gLookOnTv2": "Subtitle position: covering the game subtitle, above it, below it, or fixed at the bottom of the screen.",
  "gLookOnTv3": "Background darkness: how dark the black box behind the text is. Keep it high if you are covering the game subtitle.",
  "gTroubleTitle": "Troubleshooting",
  "gTroubleSubtitle": "Common situations",
  "gQ1": "Translation does not start, it stays at \"Connecting to the PS5\"",
  "gQ1A1": "Is the PS5 on? If it is in rest mode, enable waking as described in \"Prepare the PS5\".",
  "gQ1A2": "Is the phone on Wi-Fi and on the same network as the PS5?",
  "gQ1A3": "Is Remote Play enabled on the PS5?",
  "gQ2": "\"Remote Play is being used by another device\"",
  "gQ2A1": "The PS5 accepts only one Remote Play connection at a time. If GameTranslator on a computer or another Remote Play app is open, close it.",
  "gQ2A2": "If you just stopped it, wait a few seconds; the app retries by itself.",
  "gQ3": "My controller got detached from the TV",
  "gQ3A1": "The phone connected with the account you play on. Use Settings › PS5 › \"Change the PSN account\" to switch to the second user's account.",
  "gQ4": "The TV card stays at \"Waiting\"",
  "gQ4A1": "Is the GameTranslator app open on the TV?",
  "gQ4A2": "Is the TV on the same network as the phone? It must not be a guest network or a different router.",
  "gQ4A3": "If GameTranslator on a computer is open, close it; the TV connects to the first one it finds.",
  "gQ4A4": "If the TV app was connected to a computer before, it may be stuck on that address. Follow the \"If the TV cannot find the phone\" steps below.",
  "gTvNotFoundTitle": "If the TV cannot find the phone",
  "gRecoveryLead": "The TV app remembers the address it last connected to. If it connected to a computer before, it may keep trying that address instead of looking for the phone. Clearing the saved address makes the app scan the network again and find the phone.",
  "gRecoveryAndroidTitle": "Android TV / Google TV (TCL, Sony, Philips, Vestel…)",
  "gRecoveryAndroidStep1": "On the TV go to Settings › Apps and pick GameTranslator from the list (you may need \"Show all apps\").",
  "gRecoveryAndroidStep2": "Choose \"Clear data\" and confirm. The app is not uninstalled; only the saved address and settings are reset.",
  "gRecoveryAndroidStep3": "With translation on, open GameTranslator on the TV again.",
  "gRecoveryAndroidStep4": "Wait up to a minute; the TV card on the phone turns \"Connected\".",
  "gRecoverySamsungTitle": "Samsung and LG",
  "gRecoverySamsungStep1": "On these TVs app data cannot be cleared separately: remove GameTranslator from the TV.",
  "gRecoverySamsungStep2": "Install it again with GameTranslator on a computer (the steps in \"Prepare the TV\").",
  "gRecoverySamsungStep3": "Close GameTranslator on the computer, start translation on the phone and open the app on the TV.",
  "gRecoveryStillTitle": "If it still does not work",
  "gRecoveryStill1": "Is GameTranslator on the computer closed? If it is open, the TV connects to it.",
  "gRecoveryStill2": "Are the phone and the TV on the same Wi-Fi? If \"client isolation\" (AP isolation) is on in the router, the devices cannot see each other.",
  "gRecoveryStill3": "The HDMI setting on the TV is also reset, so press OK to open the panel and select the PS5 input again.",
  "gTroubleTip": "If you cannot solve a problem, you can copy the records in Settings › About › Log and share them.",
  "gQ5": "No game picture on the TV, the screen is black",
  "gQ5A1": "Press OK to open the panel and use left/right to select the HDMI input the PS5 is connected to.",
  "gQ5A2": "Some Android TVs do not hand the HDMI picture to another app; on those TVs the subtitle appears but the background stays black.",
  "gQ6": "No subtitle at all",
  "gQ6A1": "Are the game's own subtitles turned on?",
  "gQ6A2": "If \"Read in the frame\" on the home screen is empty, the region is in the wrong place; see \"Adjust the subtitle region\".",
  "gQ6A3": "Does the game language match the source language in Settings › Translation?",
  "gQ6A4": "If \"Send a test subtitle to the TV\" works, the TV connection is fine; the problem is in reading.",
  "gQ7": "The translation is partial or meaningless",
  "gQ7A1": "If the start or end of the sentence is missing, widen the region.",
  "gQ7A2": "If the engine is \"On device\", switch to Google or DeepL.",
  "gQ7A3": "Reading is harder with very decorative or very small fonts; increasing the subtitle size in the game and adding a background helps.",
  "gQ8": "Translation arrives late",
  "gQ8A1": "Keep the phone and the PS5 close to the router if possible; weak Wi-Fi delays the picture.",
  "gQ8A2": "With online engines the internet speed matters too.",
  "gQ9": "Translation stops when I turn the screen off",
  "gQ9A1": "The phone's battery saver may be stopping the app. On the phone go to Settings › Apps › GameTranslator › Battery and choose \"Unrestricted\".",
  "gQ9A2": "If you turned off notification permission, turn it back on; the background service runs with a notification.",
