  "tvGuideA1Title": "Open Settings on the TV",
  "tvGuideA1Body": "Press the gear (Settings) button on the TV remote. If the remote does not have one, choose the gear icon at the top right of the home screen.",
  "tvGuideA1Different": "On Google TV (newer Sony, TCL, Philips, Xiaomi models) choose the profile picture or the gear at the top right, then go to \"Settings\".",
  "tvGuideA2Title": "Open the \"About\" screen",
  "tvGuideA2Body": "Android TV: Settings › Device Preferences › About.\nGoogle TV: Settings › System › About.",
  "tvGuideA2Different": "Philips: Settings › Android Settings › Device Preferences › About.\nSony: Settings › System › About (on older models Device Preferences › About).\nTCL and Xiaomi: Settings › System › About or Device Preferences › About.\nIf you cannot find it, type \"About\" in the settings search.",
  "tvGuideA3Title": "Press the build row 7 times",
  "tvGuideA3Body": "Select the \"Android TV OS build\" row at the bottom of the list and press the remote's OK button 7 times in a row. A \"You are now a developer\" message appears.",
  "tvGuideA3Different": "The row may be called \"Build number\", \"Build\" or \"Derleme\" depending on the model. If the TV asks for a PIN, enter the TV's lock PIN. If it says \"You are already a developer\", this step is done.",
  "tvGuideA4Title": "Open developer options",
  "tvGuideA4Body": "Go back one screen with the back button. A new \"Developer options\" row has appeared under Device Preferences on Android TV and under System on Google TV; open it.",
  "tvGuideA4Different": "If you cannot see the row, leave Settings completely and enter again. If it is still missing, repeat pressing 7 times in the previous step.",
  "tvGuideA5Title": "Turn on \"USB debugging\"",
  "tvGuideA5Body": "Find \"USB debugging\" in the developer options list and turn it on; choose \"OK\" on the warning. If the list has \"Debug over network\" or \"ADB network debugging\", turn that on too.\n\nWhen the TV is on, this turns green by itself.",
  "tvGuideA5Different": "The option may be called \"Debugging (ADB)\" or \"USB debugging\". Models that only offer \"Wireless debugging\" and ask for a pairing code (e.g. Google TV Streamer) cannot be installed from the phone yet; use the USB drive path in the Guide for those.",
  "tvGuideL1Title": "Create a free LG developer account",
  "tvGuideL1Body": "Open the address below in your phone's browser, choose \"SIGN IN\" at the top right, then \"Create Account\" for a free account. You will type your e-mail and password on the TV in the next step.",
  "tvGuideL1Different": "If you already have an LG account (e.g. LG ThinQ) you can sign in with the same e-mail and password; skip this step.",
  "tvGuideL2Title": "Install the \"Developer Mode\" app on the TV",
  "tvGuideL2Body": "Open LG Content Store (Apps) on the TV, type \"Developer Mode\" in the search box and install the app.",
  "tvGuideL2Different": "If the store does not open, check that the TV is connected to the internet. On older models the store is called \"LG Store\" or \"Apps\". The app appears in English.",
  "tvGuideL3Title": "Sign in and turn on \"Dev Mode Status\"",
  "tvGuideL3Body": "Open the Developer Mode app and sign in with your LG account e-mail and password. Turn on the \"Dev Mode Status\" switch. The TV restarts by itself; wait for it to come back.\n\nWhen developer mode is on, this turns green by itself.",
  "tvGuideL3Different": "If \"Dev Mode Status\" is grey and cannot be selected, you have not signed in yet. If signing in says \"Login failed\", make sure you have verified your account's e-mail.",
  "tvGuideL4Title": "Turn on \"Key Server\"",
  "tvGuideL4Body": "After the TV comes back on, open the Developer Mode app again and turn on the \"Key Server\" switch. Leave the app on screen; if you close it, Key Server turns off too.\n\nWhen Key Server is on, this turns green by itself.",
  "tvGuideL4Different": "A 6-character \"Passphrase\" appears at the bottom left of the screen; you will type it in the next step.",
  "tvErrUnreachableAndroidTitle": "The TV did not respond",
  "tvErrUnreachableAndroidFix": "Is the TV on and on the same Wi-Fi network as the phone? \"USB debugging\" must be on in developer options. On some TVs this setting turns off when the TV restarts; turn it on and try again.",
  "tvErrUnreachableLgTitle": "The TV did not respond",
  "tvErrUnreachableLgFix": "Is the TV on and on the same Wi-Fi network as the phone? \"Dev Mode Status\" must be on in the Developer Mode app; after you turn it on the TV restarts, wait for it to come back.",
  "tvErrKeyServerOffTitle": "Key Server is off",
  "tvErrKeyServerOffFix": "Open the Developer Mode app on the TV, turn on \"Key Server\" and leave the app on screen. Then try again.",
  "tvErrWrongPassphraseTitle": "The password is not correct",
  "tvErrWrongPassphraseFix": "Type the 6-character \"Passphrase\" shown at the bottom left of the Developer Mode app on the TV again. 0 (zero) and the letter O, 1 and the letter I can be confused.",
  "tvErrKeyRefusedTitle": "The TV refused the key",
  "tvErrKeyRefusedFix": "If developer mode was turned off and on, the TV generates a new key. Turn on Key Server and type the password again.",
  "tvErrNotApprovedTitle": "Not allowed on the TV",
  "tvErrNotApprovedFix": "Try again. When the \"Allow USB debugging?\" prompt appears on the TV, tick \"Always allow from this computer\" and choose \"Allow\". The prompt waits on the TV screen for about a minute and a half.",
